00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.840
the baby who would become author virginia&nbsp;
woolf was born align virginia steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.360
on the 25th of january 1882 in hyde park&nbsp;
gate london her family background was rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.280
illustrious her grandfather said james steven had&nbsp;
authored the bill to abolish slavery in 1833. her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.200
father leslie was an author and editor founder&nbsp;
of the dictionary of national biography in 1867&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.680
leslie had married minnie thackery daughter&nbsp;
of novelist william makepeace thackery the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.760
two had a daughter laura in 1870 but five&nbsp;
years later many died of eclampsia after three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.720
years of grieving lester remarried with julia&nbsp;
duckworth a model for pre-raphaelite painters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.520
julia was also a widower and brought her&nbsp;
own three children into the household stella&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:51.120
gerald and george leslie and julia made it a point&nbsp;
to overcrowd even more their home by having four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.880
further children together vanessa born in 1879&nbsp;
later to become a painter toby born in 1880 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:04.320
a promising intellectual but he died aged just&nbsp;
26. virginia and adrian in 1883 who would become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:10.080
a psychoanalyst the four steven siblings were&nbsp;
very close and highly gifted from an early age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.800
virginia displayed a talent for writing stories&nbsp;
since the age of five penning long serials about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.680
evil spirits lurking in rubbish heaps as much&nbsp;
as virginia loved her crowded house in london&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.240
her favorite place was thailand house the&nbsp;
family summer getaway incentive's cornwall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.800
from its windows she admired the views of&nbsp;
godrevy lighthouse towering above the sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.800
or enjoyed the sounds of children playing in&nbsp;
the terraced gardens in the evenings she would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.160
compose short stories in the style of nathaniel&nbsp;
hawthorne all those memories of sentai stayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.120
with virginia well into adulthood to the point&nbsp;
that she later wrote how her entire life was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:49.040
built on that permeated by that how much so i&nbsp;
could never explain virginia's love for writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.680
and reading drew very close to her father the&nbsp;
two would spend hours together sharing books or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.160
making up stories virginia and leslie took long&nbsp;
walks together during which she taught her to dig&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.160
into the more prosaic aspects of everyday life and&nbsp;
extract fountains of poetic interest nonetheless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.640
leslie had an ambivalent attitude towards the role&nbsp;
of women as intellectuals while he encouraged his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.560
daughters to read write and learn he did not&nbsp;
believe women could lead productive literary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:17.680
or artistic careers as virginia grew older&nbsp;
she resented this patriarchal attitude but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:21.760
she had other more problematic male figures&nbsp;
in her life gerald duckworth one of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:26.560
much older half-brothers had once touched her&nbsp;
inappropriately while on holiday at some dives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:32.960
he was 18 at the time virginia was only six&nbsp;
this incident left her prone to sexual fear and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:39.680
instilled in her a resistance to aggressive&nbsp;
masculine authority this event surely clouded the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:46.400
idyllicness of her childhood but the worst was to&nbsp;
come when virginia entered her teens in may 1895&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.640
her mother julia died of heart failure julia's&nbsp;
daughter stella duckworth took on the mantle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.000
of surrogate mother but two years later she too&nbsp;
died due to complications of pregnancy with julia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.120
and stella gone there was no one else to keep&nbsp;
tabs on virginia's other half-brother george&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:05.440
according to virginia's own memoirs george would&nbsp;
visit her at night forcing himself on her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:10.880
calling her beloved but by day he would ridicule&nbsp;
her looks and called her the poor goat it was too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.760
much for a 15 year old girl to take in september&nbsp;
1897 virginia first recorded in her journal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:23.840
a wish to die this diary is lengthening indeed&nbsp;
but death would be shorter and less painful

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.960
virginia soldiered on but life kept treating&nbsp;
her like a punching bag delivering jabs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:38.960
and hooks of misery first leslie died in march&nbsp;
1904. understandably the 22 year old virginia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.040
suffered a mental collapse which led to her&nbsp;
attempting suicide by jumping out of a window&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.360
she recovered thanks to violet dickinson a&nbsp;
friend of the late stella varla was older&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.480
wise and kind just the type of motherly figure&nbsp;
the young virginia needed val nursed her back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.800
health physically and mentally along the way the&nbsp;
two developed a friendship which eventually became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.280
romantic during the same eventful year virginia&nbsp;
and her sister vanessa moved to gordon's square&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.840
in the bloomsbury area of london this was the&nbsp;
epicenter of bohemian life in london an area&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.480
rife with non-conformist intellectuals many&nbsp;
of whom gravitated around the stephen siblings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:14.880
their friends included activist and author&nbsp;
leonard wolff biographer lytton strachey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:20.480
artist roger fry economist john maynard keynes&nbsp;
and art critic clive bell who would later marry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:25.520
vanessa by moving into that milieu virginia and&nbsp;
vanessa were rejecting the habits and values&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.000
expected from two young ladies in edwardian&nbsp;
england they replaced polite small talk with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.800
discussions about politics and literature or&nbsp;
shopping trips with visits to art galleries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:40.560
and during the summer of 1905 virginia ditched&nbsp;
london's high society events for long walks across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:46.240
cornwall's countryside during that period she&nbsp;
kept a diary which became the origin of her later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.440
narrative experiments in her journal virginia&nbsp;
described how she abandoned the well-trodden roads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:57.760
to venture into barely visible paths ignoring&nbsp;
the artificial barriers imposed by man on nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.400
these ramblings were an early metaphor for her&nbsp;
later works in which the narrative ignored the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:08.480
artificial signposts imposed by traditional plot&nbsp;
lines a character's birth a marriage someone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.280
death virginia would instead explore apparently&nbsp;
insignificant moments in time which nonetheless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:18.160
can shape someone's life virginia's own&nbsp;
life however was to be shaped by the tritest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:24.800
of plot points the death of another character in&nbsp;
1906 older brother toby succumbed to typhoid while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.480
traveling in greece this event appeared&nbsp;
to ignite a steady decline in virginia's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:32.720
mental health although initially she did her&nbsp;
best to remain mentally active and productive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.440
while working as a teacher in a night school for&nbsp;
workers in south london she composed her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:43.840
short story phyllis and rosamund the plot was&nbsp;
inspired by virginia and vanessa's own experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:48.800
in london's upper middle class milo or better it&nbsp;
explored the question what would happen to two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:54.400
intelligent and ambitious sisters should they not&nbsp;
have escaped from that environment the answer was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.520
they would have been trapped in a lifeless limbo&nbsp;
like hazy figures in the background of a party two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:05.600
non-entities little more than decorative props&nbsp;
waiting for someone to marry them and yet virginia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:12.160
felt that even this state of non-existence so&nbsp;
common so typical of the era was worth recording&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.720
unlike a protagonists virginia pretty much stood&nbsp;
out from the background getting involved in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.120
the big political issues of the time such as&nbsp;
the campaign for women's rights and suffrage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:26.720
but eventually her mind deteriorated and in&nbsp;
july of 1910 virginia was committed to burley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:32.000
sanatorium in twickenham she absolutely loaded the&nbsp;
experience writing to vanessa that she saw jumping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:37.680
out of a window is there any way out this extreme&nbsp;
means of escape was not necessary however and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.160
virginia was dismissed after less than two months&nbsp;
upon a release virginia moved into a new house in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:47.520
brunswick square bloomsbury sharing lodgings with&nbsp;
her brother adrian and other friends leonard wolff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.360
was one of them and he was interested in becoming&nbsp;
more than just a friend the two got engaged and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:57.360
eventually married on august 10 1912. leonard&nbsp;
was a positive presence in virginia's life he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:01.200
helped her cope with the belts of mental illness&nbsp;
and coached her into writing her first novel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.880
the voyage out but the relationship was not&nbsp;
entirely a bed of roses leonard could not or would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:12.320
not consider virginia's sexual fears and history&nbsp;
of abuse he even considered her to be a sexual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.760
failure from her side virginia had no qualms in&nbsp;
offending leonard's background introducing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:22.880
as a penniless jew the adjustment to married&nbsp;
life and tensions that came with it may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:28.640
pushed wolfe into a period of depression in 1913.&nbsp;
her doctor sent her back to burley for another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:34.240
summer in the abyss when virginia walked out she&nbsp;
was suicidal on september 9th she consulted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:38.480
two distinguished psychiatrists dr morris&nbsp;
wright and the aptly named sir henry head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:42.480
all they could advise was a third admission to&nbsp;
burley something that virginia could not swallow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:47.520
what she did swallow instead was a massive dose of&nbsp;
bobituards she barely survived thanks to leonard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.360
and dr head who arrived at the right time and&nbsp;
pumped her stomach whilst recovering she threw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.240
herself into finalizing the voyage out published&nbsp;
in march of 1915. the novel lays out some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:01.120
main themes that wolff would explore in later work&nbsp;
such as the stifling condition of married women in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.840
early 20th century britain the voyage out was well&nbsp;
received by critics but it was not a best-seller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:09.600
moreover the stress associated with its&nbsp;
publication led virginia to suffer another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:15.280
mental breakdown a violent episode of incoherent&nbsp;
screaming followed by a comatose state this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.800
was followed by another admission at burley the&nbsp;
medical staff tried to persuade leonard and her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:27.520
family that virginia's sanity had gone worn out by&nbsp;
neuroasthenia or nervous exhaustion contemporary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:33.600
psychiatrists tend to agree that she was beset&nbsp;
by bipolar disorder instead driven by both nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:39.680
and by nurture mental illness ran in her family&nbsp;
granddad james suffered from cyclothymia which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:43.920
causes intense mood swings he had been&nbsp;
institutionalized after running naked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:49.120
through cambridge and he died in an asylum&nbsp;
her dad leslie was also cyclothymic while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.280
her mom julia suffered from depression her&nbsp;
siblings and half-siblings were not immune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:57.680
either laura leslie's daughter from his previous&nbsp;
marriage suffered from an undefined psychosis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:03.520
vanessa and adrian had cyclothymia 2 and the&nbsp;
unfortunate phobia experienced hypermanic episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:07.840
virginia's already fragile mental state was&nbsp;
further compromised by the traumatic experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:13.600
suffered since childhood the series of deaths in&nbsp;
the family and the vile sexual abuse perpetrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:19.040
by the darkworth boys and yet it would be&nbsp;
reductive to identify virginia woolf with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:25.360
a mental health condition her vitality resilience&nbsp;
and sheer willpower would not allow her to succumb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:32.080
to institutionalization she would not accept to&nbsp;
lead a life defined by malay a life adrift driven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.520
by the storms of mania or the dead calm&nbsp;
of depression against all medical opinion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:42.720
by november 1915 virginia had recovered and was&nbsp;
ready to leave burley after 20 years of half-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.960
she was ready to throw open the curtains and&nbsp;
take on the most productive period of her life

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:56.080
after virginia's recovery leonard was still&nbsp;
worried that the effect of writing would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:00.080
cause her to have another breakdown and looked&nbsp;
for a distraction for her as virginia had an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:04.480
interest in printing and binding books by&nbsp;
hand he ordered a hand printing machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:09.920
this activity started as a hobby but soon it&nbsp;
became a business hogarth press the wolves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:14.080
initially used hogarth press to publish their&nbsp;
own works this was a relief for virginia who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:19.120
dreaded submitting a manuscript to the prong eyes&nbsp;
of editors and publishers soon they expanded their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:24.160
catalogue to include small and experimental works&nbsp;
likely to be rejected by commercial publishers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.800
these included writings by their friends iam&nbsp;
foster and john mayne at keynes but also by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:35.440
sigmund freud and t.s eliot in 1919 virginia&nbsp;
released her short story q gardens via hogarth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:40.800
press the story contrasts the aimless meandering&nbsp;
of eight characters against the purposeful march&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.600
of a snail and attracted the attention of the&nbsp;
times literary supplement the favorable review&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.880
led to hundreds of orders and commercial success&nbsp;
so much so that leonard and virginia had to forego&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:54.960
the hand printing press and hire a commercial&nbsp;
printer while hogarth press was taking off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.960 --> 00:13:00.720
virginia was completing her second novel night and&nbsp;
day published in october of 1919. wolff explores&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.680
again the theme of women who struggle to achieve&nbsp;
their full potential locked in a society who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:11.360
accepts them only as wives and daughters the main&nbsp;
character catherine actively opposes her emilio of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:16.080
upper class intellectuals first by embracing&nbsp;
mathematics instead of poetry and then by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:22.160
rejecting the courtship of a poet as she pursues&nbsp;
the love of an upstart solicitor night and day was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:26.880
the first in a series of writings in which wolf&nbsp;
shaped the defining characteristics of the modern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:32.320
novel she introduced the principle that writers&nbsp;
did not need sensational events to propel a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:37.920
or develop a character an ordinary mind on an&nbsp;
ordinary day was worthy of being narrated in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:43.520
novel she aimed to capture the moments of being&nbsp;
these ordinary minds climatic inward events or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:49.040
epiphanies that may strike her characters while&nbsp;
they conduct the most mundane activities morph&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:54.720
adopted these principles in a follow-up novels&nbsp;
jacob's room of 1922 and mrs dalloway published&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.720 --> 00:14:00.080
in 1925. the latter novel takes place over a&nbsp;
single day in june a concept inspired by jane's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:05.200
joyce ulysses mrs clarissa delaway roams london&nbsp;
looking to buy flowers for a party that she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:10.320
throwing she's renowned amongst london's high&nbsp;
society as bright and a lively hostess although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:16.000
she is not entirely satisfied with her own life&nbsp;
clarisse's urban travels are mirrored by her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.320
internal meanderings as she questions the&nbsp;
meaning of her own existence and reminisces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:25.200
about her first love peter and about her lone&nbsp;
homosexual experience wolff then introduces the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:30.320
second main character septimus warren smith a&nbsp;
world war one veteran afflicted by shell shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:35.920
smith is plagued by hallucination by an inability&nbsp;
to feel emotions and worst of all by poor medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:41.440
treatment the two never meet but during the party&nbsp;
clarissa overhears a guest telling how septimus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:46.960
committed suicide earlier that day by jumping out&nbsp;
of a window despite this tragic revelation the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:52.880
novel ends on an optimistic note by reflecting on&nbsp;
septimus's suicide clarissa finds a new interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:57.840
in the beauty of life and reconnects with former&nbsp;
love peter many contemporary critics and readers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:03.200
consider mrs dalloway as wolff's best novel&nbsp;
but it's a close tie with a follow-up title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:09.120
to the lighthouse published in may 1927. the&nbsp;
book is divided into three sections the window&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:14.160
time passes and the lighthouse the first section&nbsp;
the window takes place over a single day the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:19.200
ramses are at their holiday home on the isle of&nbsp;
skye stand in for the stevens's own retreat in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:23.600
cornwall one of the children james is planning a&nbsp;
boat trip to a lighthouse but his father talks him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:28.720
out of it claiming bad weather the second and&nbsp;
shorter section time passes covers 10 years of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:34.160
events including world war one during this period&nbsp;
the ramsey house a symbol for civilization rots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:40.800
away abandoned the house was left the house was&nbsp;
deserted it was left like a shell on a sand hill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:47.440
to fill with dry salt grains now that life had&nbsp;
left it in this section wolff hastily introduces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:52.800
the death of important characters as quick edits&nbsp;
in between square brackets our favorite example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:59.200
is a shell exploded 20 or 30 young men were blown&nbsp;
up in france among them andrew ramsay whose death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:04.960
mercifully was instantaneous in the final section&nbsp;
the lighthouse james finally completes his trip to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.960
the lighthouse 10 years after originally&nbsp;
planned as with many of wolff's novels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:14.240
it's difficult to pinpoint a single key theme&nbsp;
the more evident ones are the nature of time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:20.000
how patterns of delay repetition and inaction&nbsp;
can affect one's life despite its complexity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:25.520
the novel was well received by critics and readers&nbsp;
much to the surprise of the author on june 6 1927&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:30.640
she noted in a diary they don't laugh at me any&nbsp;
longer possibly i shall be a celebrated writer

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:42.960
the celebrated writer defied all expectations with&nbsp;
the next work orlando a biography of 1928. almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:48.720
fantasy in tone the novel features the titular&nbsp;
character who switches gender at a whim and lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:53.840
through centuries of british history the novel&nbsp;
defies the traditional linear concept of time as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.840 --> 00:17:00.000
the protagonist accumulates memories each of them&nbsp;
becoming a wormhole transporting her or him back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.440
to a different period but orlando can also be read&nbsp;
as a fictional biography of a real life character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:12.320
poet novelist and horticulturalist vita sackville&nbsp;
west vita and virginia had first met in 1923&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:17.760
struck up a friendship and took holidays together&nbsp;
in france and italy virginia idolized vita and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:22.880
their friendship developed into a short romance&nbsp;
which became physical only on two occasions the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:28.240
unstoppable wolf hit the bookshelves again the&nbsp;
following year with the essay a room of one zone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:33.200
one of her most celebrated feminist writings in&nbsp;
this work virginia addresses the pressures which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:38.000
deny the intellectual and professional development&nbsp;
of women the confinement to the domestic sphere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.400
conformity to the patriarch but most of all the&nbsp;
inability for women to have their own income&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:48.720
and privacy hence the title a woman must have&nbsp;
money and a room of her own if she has to ride&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:54.560
the essay also looks at how history is written&nbsp;
as a succession of wars waged by powerful kings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.560 --> 00:18:00.000
and generals wolff invites readers to consider&nbsp;
a counter-historiography instead one focused on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:04.480
those women excluded from historical records&nbsp;
generations of mothers and daughters who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:09.840
maintained domestic order and social peace which&nbsp;
were regularly destroyed by militaristic thugs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:15.440
the next effort was 1931's the waves virginia's&nbsp;
most experimental work the narrative is structured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:21.280
as six soliloquies voiced by three men and three&nbsp;
women over a single day they are all coping with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:26.960
the death of a dear friend the characters do&nbsp;
not show any external expression of grief but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:31.200
the author reveals their personalities&nbsp;
through their internal stream of consciousness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:36.080
in 1932 the writer launched into another ambitious&nbsp;
project which occupied her for the next five years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:41.680
this was the years a family chronicle which became&nbsp;
wolf's best-selling work during a lifetime here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:46.960
will follows the extended pargdar family heavily&nbsp;
influenced by our own each section starts with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.960
a sweeping narration describing the sky&nbsp;
over britain or london in particular before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:55.680
zooming in to the consciousness of a particular&nbsp;
character their seemingly random activities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.680 --> 00:19:00.080
dialogues and thoughts take the reader through&nbsp;
50 years of british history and institutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:05.120
analyzing how they've shaped the consciousness of&nbsp;
individuals the initial draft included a running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:10.960
social commentary on the condition of women which&nbsp;
virginia edited out and then published in 1938 as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:16.560
